==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[hifalutin]], [[highfaluting]], [[high falutin]]

===Etymology===
Alteration of {{term|high-fluting|lang=en}}. In his book, ''The Adventure of English'', Melvyn Bragg records that in a nascent America, when the well-to-do travelled by steamboat, said passengers were referred to as highfalutin due to the high fluted funnels on the boats. Compare [[riffraff]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌhaɪ.fəˈlu.tɨn/|/ˈhaɪ.fəˌlu.tɨn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-highfalutin.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|US|informal|lang=en}} Self-[[important]], [[pompous]]; [[arrogant]] or [[egotistical]]; tending to [[show off]] or hold oneself in unduly high [[regard]].
#: ''It's only a matter of time before some '''highfalutin''' developer builds a huge hotel and ruins the scenery.''

====Synonyms====
* [[hoity-toity]]

